        "scope": "in_scope",
        "statement": "For a real symmetric irreducible tridiagonal matrix with exactly one\nnonzero diagonal entry, at $\\ell$, nSSP holds if and only if the\ntwo branches obtained by deleting $\\ell$ have disjoint spectra.\nIn particular, if every edge has weight $1$ and the loop has any\nnonzero value, then nSSP holds exactly when $\\gcd(\\ell,n+1)=1$.",
